# Technical Drawing Visual Rules (Packing Canvas)

## Specialized GUI Area
- Apply only to the 2D packing visualization surface: `QGraphicsScene` / `QGraphicsView` and related paint or item classes that render the pallet (bin), placed boxes, labels, and dimensions.

## Visual Language
- The scene must look like a clean architectural/technical drawing: neutral grayscale lines, low-saturation accents, high readability, no playful gradients, no cartoon styling.
- Use a white or very light gray background (`#FAFAF8` to `#FFFFFF`).

## Stroke Hierarchy (Mandatory)
- Bin outer boundary: solid stroke `2.0 px`, color `#2F2F2F`.
- Box outer boundary: solid stroke `1.4 px`, color `#4A4A4A`.
- Internal dimension lines and extension lines: `0.9 px`, color `#7A7A7A`.
- Auxiliary grid (if enabled): `0.5 px`, color `#E2E2E2`.
- Keep this hierarchy strict; never use equal line weight for all elements.

## Dimensioning Rules (Mandatory)
- Draw dimensions inside each placed box, never outside the box and never across neighboring boxes.
- Show width and height with orthogonal dimension lines and arrowheads.
- Use text format `W x H` (example: `1200 x 800`), font size `9-10 px`, color `#555555`.
- Minimum text padding from box edge: `4 px`.
- If the box is too small to host readable dimensions, hide dimensions for that box (do not overflow).

## Overlap and Z-Order Rules (Mandatory)
- Box geometry must never overlap with other boxes; enforce non-overlap in both solver output and render pass.
- Dimension text or dimension lines must never draw over another box.
- Use z-order: grid < bin < boxes < dimensions < labels/markers.
- Before final paint, run collision checks for label bounding rectangles; if collision occurs, reduce detail (hide secondary label) instead of drawing over content.

## Color and Fill Rules
- Box fill: very light neutral tint (`#F3F3F1` to `#ECECE9`) with opacity `0.85-0.95`.
- Keep strong contrast between outlines and fills; outlines must remain clearly legible at 100% zoom.
- Optional placement marker dots may use muted green (`#BFDFAE`) at low opacity only.

## Interaction and Scaling
- All strokes and text must remain legible between 80% and 200% zoom.
- Avoid sub-pixel jitter: align key geometry to pixel grid where possible.
- On resize/zoom, preserve line hierarchy and do not auto-scale line widths into indistinguishable values.
